Given a test in which the items whose parameters  in the 3PL type are known, how to obtain the latent traits of the test takers with the data frame of their response? More specific, suppose there are n items and the vectors:
a (of length n) - storing the discriminating parameters of the items;
d (of length n) - storing the difficulty parameters of the items; and
g (of length n) - storing the guess parameters of the items.

And a data frame answers that stores the answers of the N  persons that take the test, in format of LST7 after the execution of expand.table. How to obtain the latent trait of each person without passing to the mirt function? I tried the fscore function, but I could not make it happen without the use of the mirt function.

